{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyMaximum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyMaximum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_max_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_max_value","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L263-L276","doc":"**The maximum VALUE is exactly `Cl₂(π/3)`.**\n\n`qou-7y3g` records `Vol(4₁) = 2 × V_tet` numerically with\n`V_tet = Cl₂(π/3)`; this supplies the `V_tet` side exactly.  The bridge to the\nmanifold's volume is the geometric content and is NOT supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_isMaxOn_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_isMaxOn_regular","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L235-L261","doc":"**T4 — the regular triple `(π/3, π/3, π/3)` maximises the Lobachevsky volume\nsum, and is the ONLY maximiser.**\n\nMilnor's theorem, in its analytic form: this is a statement about the function\n`Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(π - α - β)`, and becomes the geometric statement only modulo\n`qou-idvt` T2 (open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.swap_snd_thd_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.swap_snd_thd_mem","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L228-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.swap_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.swap_mem","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L224-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_swap_snd_thd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_swap_snd_thd","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L218-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_swap","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L213-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.exists_isMaxOn_angleSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.exists_isMaxOn_angleSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L191-L209","doc":"**A maximiser exists, and it lies in the OPEN simplex.**\n\nCompactness gives a maximum on the closed simplex; the boundary value `0` and\nthe strictly positive regular value push it into the interior.  This is the step\nthat makes T3's uniqueness non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_regular_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_regular_pos","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L178-L187","doc":"At the regular point the value is `3Λ(π/3) = Cl₂(π/3) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_eq_zero_of_not_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_eq_zero_of_not_mem","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L154-L176","doc":"**The volume sum vanishes on the boundary of the closed simplex.**\nEach of the three degenerate faces kills it, via `Lob_pi_sub`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.continuous_volChart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.continuous_volChart","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L146-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.isCompact_closedSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.isCompact_closedSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L138-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.isClosed_closedSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.isClosed_closedSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L129-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex_subset_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex_subset_closed","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L125-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.closedSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.closedSimplex","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L121-L123","doc":"The CLOSED angle simplex.  Compact, so a maximum exists on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_duplication","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_duplication","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L98-L117","doc":"**The duplication identity `Λ(2a) = 2Λ(a) + 2Λ(a + π/2)`.**\n\nThis is the `n = 2` case of Milnor's multiplication identity, and the exact\nsubstitution his orthoscheme computation makes to collapse\n`(Λ(π/2 + a) + Λ(2a) + Λ(π/2 - a) - Λ(0))/4` to `Λ(a)/2`.\n\nProof: `Cl_2_duplication` at `θ = 2a` gives `Cl₂(4a) = 2Cl₂(2a) - 2Cl₂(π - 2a)`,\nand `Cl_2_two_pi_sub` at `π - 2a` gives `Cl₂(π + 2a) = -Cl₂(π - 2a)`, which is\nprecisely the term needed to match. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_add_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_add_pi","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L92-L96","doc":"**`Λ` has period `π`** -- Milnor's Appendix, Lemma 1. Immediate from `Cl₂`'s\n`2π`-periodicity, since `Λ(t) = Cl₂(2t)/2` doubles the argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_pi_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.Lob_pi_sub","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**`Λ(π - t) = -Λ(t)`** -- antisymmetry about `π/2`, from `Cl₂`'s\nantisymmetry about `π`.  This is what makes the volume sum vanish on every\ndegenerate face of the simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.continuous_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.continuous_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyMaximum.lean#L68-L71","doc":"**`Λ` is continuous**, inherited from `Cl₂`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}